  "scope": "The browser installed lane authenticates the ordinary mutual recursive checked-record selection for node-javascript, node-typescript, browser-javascript, browser-react, browser-worker. Original inputs, exact failures, preserved rejected values, recovery and proof-free results are retained; independently reproduced packages are installed without author sources and replayed after relocation where the host permits it. The archive authenticates local Linux x64 Node, strict TypeScript, Chromium, Firefox and WebKit execution; it does not claim hosted-runner acceptance. Acceptance covers the tested finite mutually recursive Envelope and Branch records/variants, transparent aliases, Array and Option copies; host cycles are rejected and traversal is bounded. Callback, owned, asynchronous and retained-identity positions remain separate requirements. Browser binaries, framework archives and generated deployments are represented by recorded identities and observations rather than copied. Constructor dispatch counts and peak memory remain unmeasured. Recursive checked-record acceptance covers the tested Packet self-cycle and Envelope ↔ Step mutual cycle, their aliases, Array/Option wrappers, active branches, Nat Subtype constructors and Fin 3 fields in copied parameters, results and fields. It does not establish generic recursive records, other recursive graph shapes, value-carrying receiver-dependent fields, other index kinds, open dependent or zero-payload records, callbacks or owned positions.",
