  "scope": "The perl installed lane authenticates the ordinary recursive recursive checked-record selection for perl. Original inputs, exact failures, preserved rejected values, recovery and proof-free results are retained; independently reproduced packages are installed without author sources and replayed after relocation where the host permits it. These are local Linux x64/glibc 2.36 observations with an explicit 2.36 package floor. The dedicated hosted workflow retains the production 2.38 floor. Each ordinary/reviewed recursive/mutual cell was built twice in independent author roots, then installed through prebuilt-only and local XS compilation on threaded and unthreaded Perl 5.36.3 and 5.38.2. Every installation ran an unchanged caller before and after moving the complete installed tree, for sixteen executions per cell. Recursive executions recorded 1,709 checks, 144 Lean rejections, 79 host rejections, 95 recoveries and 496 snapshots; mutual executions recorded 1,734 checks, 144 Lean rejections, 81 host rejections, 97 recoveries and 502 snapshots. The exact fixtures cover recursive records, mutual record/variant cycles, aliases, ordered fields, active branches, checked Nat subtypes, Fin 3 fields, exact depth and cycle failures, input preservation, recovery and constructor-free results. The archive retains every non-binary producer record, package-set receipts, checksum sidecars, TAP, verification and the producer source closure. Prepared component and runtime CPAN archive bytes are omitted after the original checker authenticated their byte lengths and SHA-256 identities. Proof fields do not appear in generated Perl classes or result values. Runtime work includes explicit Fin, Subtype and checked-record validation, not proof removal. This archive establishes only the four named Perl cells. Other hosts, owned values, callbacks, open dependent shapes and broader recursive forms remain separate work; this archive does not itself promote documented support. Recursive checked-record acceptance covers the tested Packet self-cycle and Envelope ↔ Step mutual cycle, their aliases, Array/Option wrappers, active branches, Nat Subtype constructors and Fin 3 fields in copied parameters, results and fields. It does not establish generic recursive records, other recursive graph shapes, value-carrying receiver-dependent fields, other index kinds, open dependent or zero-payload records, callbacks or owned positions.",
