  "scope": "The php installed lane authenticates the ordinary mutual recursive checked-record selection for php-native. Original inputs, exact failures, preserved rejected values, recovery and proof-free results are retained; independently reproduced packages are installed without author sources and replayed after relocation where the host permits it. The fixtures cover the tested self-recursive Packet graph and mutually recursive Envelope/Step graph; runtime values are finite and bounded. Checked fields are limited to Fin 3 and the tested Nat Subtype constructors. Acceptance covers weak and strict callers before and after relocation through the exact retained Composer package and PHP FFI closure. Generic, inherited, open dependent and zero-payload records remain separate work. Callbacks, resources and explicitly owned or borrowed positions remain separate work. The packages declare a glibc 2.38 floor and were executed by the hosted Ubuntu 24.04 runner on glibc 2.39; this does not claim execution on a 2.38 host. PHP constructor dispatch and peak memory are unmeasured; Lean, PHP, Composer, the operating system and native compiler remain trusted toolchain inputs. Recursive checked-record acceptance covers the tested Packet self-cycle and Envelope ↔ Step mutual cycle, their aliases, Array/Option wrappers, active branches, Nat Subtype constructors and Fin 3 fields in copied parameters, results and fields. It does not establish generic recursive records, other recursive graph shapes, value-carrying receiver-dependent fields, other index kinds, open dependent or zero-payload records, callbacks or owned positions.",
