  "scope": "The php-wasm installed lane authenticates the reviewed recursive recursive checked-record selection for php-wasm. Original inputs, exact failures, preserved rejected values, recovery and proof-free results are retained; independently reproduced packages are installed without author sources and replayed after relocation where the host permits it. The fixtures cover the self-recursive Packet graph and the mutually recursive Envelope/Step graph with Option and Array carriers. Checked fields are limited to Fin 3 and the tested plusOne/plusTwo Nat Subtype constructors. The PHP-Wasm caller reuses the native-PHP caller and oracle byte for byte; acceptance does not follow from native PHP and every cell runs inside wasm32 PHP-Wasm. Generic, inherited, open dependent and zero-payload records, callbacks and explicitly owned positions remain separate work. Consumer PHP source remains required when the installed package executes. These local Linux x64 runs do not establish hosted release-floor acceptance. Compiler, operating-system, browser, Node, PHP, Composer and npm distributions remain trusted. Constructor dispatch and peak memory are unmeasured. Recursive checked-record acceptance covers the tested Packet self-cycle and Envelope ↔ Step mutual cycle, their aliases, Array/Option wrappers, active branches, Nat Subtype constructors and Fin 3 fields in copied parameters, results and fields. It does not establish generic recursive records, other recursive graph shapes, value-carrying receiver-dependent fields, other index kinds, open dependent or zero-payload records, callbacks or owned positions.",
