  "scope": "The rust installed lane authenticates the ordinary mutual recursive checked-record selection for rust. Original inputs, exact failures, preserved rejected values, recovery and proof-free results are retained; independently reproduced packages are installed without author sources and replayed after relocation where the host permits it. The fixtures cover the tested self-recursive Packet graph and mutually recursive Envelope/Step graph; runtime values are finite and bounded. Checked fields are limited to Fin 3 and the tested Nat Subtype constructors. Acceptance covers the exact identities, aliases, active branches, traversal limits, diagnostics, recovery paths and positions exercised by the immutable Rust caller. Generic, inherited, open dependent and zero-payload records remain separate work. Callbacks, resources and explicitly owned or borrowed positions remain separate work. These local Linux x64/glibc 2.36 runs do not establish hosted release-floor acceptance. The original four selections were individually authenticated after serial execution; their separate TAP streams do not encode cross-selection timestamps. Constructor dispatch and peak memory are unmeasured; Rust, Cargo, the system linker and glibc remain trusted toolchain inputs. Recursive checked-record acceptance covers the tested Packet self-cycle and Envelope ↔ Step mutual cycle, their aliases, Array/Option wrappers, active branches, Nat Subtype constructors and Fin 3 fields in copied parameters, results and fields. It does not establish generic recursive records, other recursive graph shapes, value-carrying receiver-dependent fields, other index kinds, open dependent or zero-payload records, callbacks or owned positions.",
