  "command": "node --test tests/recursive-checked-record-wit.test.mjs",
  "scope": "The wit installed lane authenticates the ordinary recursive recursive checked-record selection for wit-wasi. Original inputs, exact failures, preserved rejected values, recovery and proof-free results are retained; independently reproduced packages are installed without author sources and replayed after relocation where the host permits it. The fixtures cover self-recursive Packet and mutual Envelope/Step groups with Option and Array carriers. Checked fields are limited to Fin 3 and the tested plusOne/plusTwo Nat Subtype constructors. Each package is a copied-graph WIT component whose native host forwards exact refinement diagnostics as the final Wasmtime error cause; callbacks, resources and owned positions remain separate work. The component requires its packaged native Lean host and is not a standalone WASI command. Accepted cells come from serial attempts r2 and r3 at one frozen revision; r1 and the r2 reviewed-mutual cell refused on disk and load guards and are retained only as observations. These local Linux x64/glibc 2.36 runs do not establish hosted release-floor acceptance. Constructor dispatch and peak memory are unmeasured. Recursive checked-record acceptance covers the tested Packet self-cycle and Envelope ↔ Step mutual cycle, their aliases, Array/Option wrappers, active branches, Nat Subtype constructors and Fin 3 fields in copied parameters, results and fields. It does not establish generic recursive records, other recursive graph shapes, value-carrying receiver-dependent fields, other index kinds, open dependent or zero-payload records, callbacks or owned positions.",
